1xb8|n|The state or quality of being stable, or firm; steadiness; firmness; strength to stand without being moved or overthrown; as, the stability of a structure; the stability of a throne or a constitution. ; Steadiness or firmness of character, firmness of resolution or purpose; the quality opposite to fickleness, irresolution, or inconstancy; constancy; steadfastness; as, a man of little stability, or of unusual stability. ; Fixedness; -- as opposed to fluidity.	a:1oc3,12,6~1oc3,12,6	V:1q0g,17,4;29js,6,1;21ih,6,4~21ih,6,4;1q0g,17,4;29js,6,1	n:xfw,0,2~xfw,0,2	N:182x,40,7;i84,22,4;19y,7,3~182x,40,7;i84,22,4;19y,7,3
