1xcu|a|That stagnates; not flowing; not running in a current or steam; motionless; hence, impure or foul from want of motion; as, a stagnant lake or pond; stagnant blood in the veins. ; Not active or brisk; dull; as, business in stagnant.	j:162f,99,14;285t,65,7;1td,61,11~162f,99,14;1td,61,11;285t,65,7	e:1erj,50,3;e9a,39,3~1erj,50,3;e9a,39,3
