1xzs|v|To change the place of in any manner; to move. ; To disturb the relative position of the particles of, as of a liquid, by passing something through it; to agitate; as, to stir a pudding with a spoon. ; To bring into debate; to agitate; to moot. ; To incite to action; to arouse; to instigate; to prompt; to excite. ; To move; to change one's position. ; To be in motion; to be active or bustling; to exert or busy one's self. ; To become the object of notice; to be on foot. ; To rise, or be up, in the morning.	d:1431,10,5;21r7,4,3~1431,10,5;21r7,4,3	D:ujr,73,1;28e3,11,1~ujr,73,1;28e3,11,1
