1y0t|v|To lay up; to put aside for future use; to store, as merchandise, and the like. ; To provide with material requisites; to store; to fill; to supply; as, to stock a warehouse, that is, to fill it with goods; to stock a farm, that is, to supply it with cattle and tools; to stock land, that is, to occupy it with a permanent growth, especially of grass. ; To suffer to retain milk for twenty-four hours or more previous to sale, as cows. ; To put in the stocks.	s:16qr,14,1~16qr,14,1
