1y71|n|Race; stock; generation; descent; family. ; Hereditary character, quality, or disposition. ; Rank; a sort. ; The act of straining, or the state of being strained. ; A violent effort; an excessive and hurtful exertion or tension, as of the muscles; as, he lifted the weight with a strain; the strain upon a ship's rigging in a gale; also, the hurt or injury resulting; a sprain. ; A change of form or dimensions of a solid or liquid mass, produced by a stress. ; A portion of music divided off by a double bar; a complete musical period or sentence; a movement, or any rounded subdivision of a movement. ; Any sustained note or movement; a song; a distinct portion of an ode or other poem; also, the pervading note, or burden, of a song, poem, oration, book, etc.; theme; motive; manner; style; also, a course of action or conduct; as, he spoke in a noble strain; there was a strain of woe in his story; a strain of trickery appears in his career. ; Turn; tendency; inborn disposition. Cf. 1st Strain.	a:27hf,95,4;2311,91,5;5y0,91,2;f6r,90,4;22tu,88,6;1pla,81,12;5dj,76,2;1gtt,74,3;25aa,73,4;19kp,65,6;5zy,64,9;27fa,60,2;1pvk,60,7;11il,55,1;luv,50,3~1pla,81,12;5zy,64,9;1gnj,18,8;1m36,23,7;1pvk,60,7;19kp,65,6;qmh,14,6;22tu,88,6;1imv,11,6;vrg,11,6;16i4,4,6;1egm,5,5;17kp,19,5;18k8,35,5;1593,7,5	v:1pa3,70,2;5dj,66,1;oby,58,2;e88,52,3;92r,39,5;10te,34,5;1n32,33,7;1osr,28,5;bas,26,4;a5a,25,2;1lhg,11,3;bag,5,4;uun,4,4;1n21,4,4~1n32,33,7;1osr,28,5;92r,39,5;10te,34,5;uun,4,4;1n21,4,4;bas,26,4;bag,5,4;1lhg,11,3;e88,52,3;oby,58,2;1pa3,70,2;a5a,25,2;5dj,66,1	V:qh3,65,4;pvr,56,6;axu,53,4;ay5,48,5;e6b,28,5;2874,26,2;bah,25,3;ugx,16,2;1n21,4,4~pvr,56,6;e6b,28,5;ay5,48,5;axu,53,4;qh3,65,4;1n21,4,4;bah,25,3;2874,26,2;ugx,16,2	n:5y0,91,2;11il,70,3;27fa,70,4;14kr,66,6;29kr,61,5;26i2,61,4;qqk,59,29;1c1w,59,3;2874,44,7;27hi,43,6;14r5,40,9;26pg,40,4;ip0,37,3;qh4,34,5;2bz,33,3~qqk,59,29;14r5,40,9;1b4b,15,7;2874,44,7;27hi,43,6;1ow4,18,6;14kr,66,6;yja,9,5;29kr,61,5;qh4,34,5;14r2,11,4;26i2,61,4;26pg,40,