1yc0|n|Strained; drawn close; tight; as, a strict embrace; a strict ligature. ; Tense; not relaxed; as, a strict fiber. ; Exact; accurate; precise; rigorously nice; as, to keep strict watch; to pay strict attention. ; Governed or governing by exact rules; observing exact rules; severe; rigorous; as, very strict in observing the Sabbath. ; Rigidly; interpreted; exactly limited; confined; restricted; as, to understand words in a strict sense. ; Upright, or straight and narrow; -- said of the shape of the plants or their flower clusters.	a:1fa0,16,1~1fa0,16,1	V:16mu,19,2~16mu,19,2	N:rrr,5,2~rrr,5,2
