1yda|n|A line, or long, narrow division of anything of a different color or structure from the ground; hence, any linear variation of color or structure; as, a stripe, or streak, of red on a green ground; a raised stripe. ; A pattern produced by arranging the warp threads in sets of alternating colors, or in sets presenting some other contrast of appearance. ; A strip, or long, narrow piece attached to something of a different color; as, a red or blue stripe sewed upon a garment. ; A stroke or blow made with a whip, rod, scourge, or the like, such as usually leaves a mark. ; A long, narrow discoloration of the skin made by the blow of a lash, rod, or the like. ; Color indicating a party or faction; hence, distinguishing characteristic; sign; likeness; sort; as, persons of the same political stripe. ; The chevron on the coat of a noncommissioned officer.	a:1owy,80,4;29l4,65,6;1r7d,58,3;17ge,58,5;1mz8,56,3;274e,54,7;28oj,46,7;vs8,44,4;1op7,41,6;hrg,41,4;7yj,38,10;89s,38,3;1iym,12,1;1ces,8,2;1t2s,6,2~7yj,38,10;274e,54,7;28oj,46,7;29l4,65,6;1op7,41,6;17ge,58,5;vs8,44,4;1owy,80,4;hrg,41,4;1mz8,56,3;89s,38,3;1r7d,58,3;1t2s,6,2;1ces,8,2;1iym,12,1	v:1v69,104,1;1a51,33,5;vs8,24,1~1a51,33,5;1v69,104,1;vs8,24,1	V:vb8,18,3~vb8,18,3	n:1v69,120,3;1eai,63,4;1nwi,59,11;vu4,56,4;1r7d,52,2;15mc,36,3;k2p,32,2;hrg,31,2;1iym,22,2;1op7,16,1~1nwi,59,11;1eai,63,4;vu4,56,4;15mc,36,3;1v69,120,3;1iym,22,2;hrg,31,2;1r7d,52,2;k2p,32,2;1op7,16,1	N:1gwb,49,6;9y9,34,4;1v0x,21,6;va,11,1~1v0x,21,6;1gwb,49,6;9y9,34,4;va,11,1
